[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-81439"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=2{e}^{2t}$, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x={e}^{2}$ and velocity $v={e}^{2}$ when $t=1$, calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 2{e}^{2t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)={e}^{2}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2} & ={e}^{2(1)}+C \\\\ {e}^{2} & ={e}^{2}+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)={e}^{2t}.$ \n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{2t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K,$ we use the fact that $x(1)={e}^{2}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(1)}+K \\\\ {e}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}+K \\\\ K & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-351554/field-1/5d22e7324e318bf2f8183d22d2316b99bf7ccf6dd8ba651c94cf92adc8d43833" :answer/id #uuid "b7a48b8d-9bde-546e-bb8f-b07e755fe2db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7t+58" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351554/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "95e093ee-f3aa-5a6f-91aa-e54b066389f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351554/field-1/5d22e7324e318bf2f8183d22d2316b99bf7ccf6dd8ba651c94cf92adc8d43833" :answer-field/choices ["q-351554/field-1/5d22e7324e318bf2f8183d22d2316b99bf7ccf6dd8ba651c94cf92adc8d43833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351554" :question/id #uuid "c66c33a8-1671-5b74-a094-92b58002d291" :question/math-academy-id "q-351554" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=-7,$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=30$ when $t=4,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int -7\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-7t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(4)=30.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30 & =-7(4)+C \\\\ 30 & =-28+C \\\\ C & =58.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=-7t+58.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351554/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351554"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351724/field-1/7288163923bb9dc3b82de625939afc709221fbbad464503979a201867fb85296" :answer/id #uuid "a4cd12a8-3168-55fa-b6c1-5969ee91eba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\cot(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186289955 :answer-field/choices ["q-351724/field-1/7288163923bb9dc3b82de625939afc709221fbbad464503979a201867fb85296"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351732/field-1/9ae7283f1a4fbf8680cf6be57d8d7345d0d1e6cc71a01cc78adceac4576195e5" :answer/id #uuid "b07766a8-079c-5679-8ae1-5d8213f75331" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{-2t}}{4}+\\frac{t}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351732/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cc7f01f-5253-59ca-b5a0-d11b6ff6da61" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351732/field-1/9ae7283f1a4fbf8680cf6be57d8d7345d0d1e6cc71a01cc78adceac4576195e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-351732/field-1/9ae7283f1a4fbf8680cf6be57d8d7345d0d1e6cc71a01cc78adceac4576195e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351732" :question/id #uuid "d60b6719-04f5-5e7d-a166-15c23dff2e1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-351732" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)={e}^{-2t},$ where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=0$ and velocity $v=0$ when $t=0,$ the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{-2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(0)=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\frac{1}{-2}{e}^{0}+C \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{1}{2}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{1}{2}t+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K$, we use the fact that $x(0)=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{0}+\\frac{1}{2}(0)+K \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{4}+K \\\\ K & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{1}{2}t-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351732/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43e68991-37f0-543e-a4da-b78b395a8494"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351732"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
